Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 09:22:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Test Order: redesign for receptionist workflow speed (UX
 review)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Addresses the UX review point-by-point:

- Patient summary promoted to the visual anchor: sticky, 56px avatar,
  22px/700 name, accent patient ID, a real 'Registered' status chip,
  a visit-type badge, and the same icon-prefixed field band used on
  Reports/Sample Collection for cross-page consistency.
- Search workspace: Recently Ordered chip row, segmented (38px,
  icon-prefixed) category filter instead of bootstrap-style pills,
  and a clearer search placeholder.
- Popular Tests are now action cards (name/price/'Frequently
  Ordered' badge, hover reveals an 'Add Test' cta) instead of tags.
- New Frequently Ordered Packages section (Diabetes / Kidney /
  Thyroid / Wellness) fills the dead space between Popular Tests
  and the catalogue, one click adds every test in the bundle.
- New 'Patients Also Order' smart suggestions, driven by a static
  cross-sell map keyed off whatever is currently selected.
- LabTest model extended with tubeType/sampleType/prep so every row
  in the catalogue shows tube type, sample type, TAT and any prep
  instructions (e.g. fasting) without a second screen.
- Test rows: 72px height (was 60px), selection now reads as a green
  left border + soft highlight + animated check, not just a tint.
- Order summary panel split into four distinct cards (Selected
  Tests / Priority / Summary / Actions) instead of one long card.
- Selected-test rows show category and a trash icon.
- Summary expands to Subtotal / Discount / Tax / Grand Total (was
  Tests/TAT/Total), using the discount plumbing billing already has.
- Priority is now three descriptive cards (Routine – Normal queue,
  Urgent – Priority queue, STAT – Immediate) instead of toggle
  buttons, with a stronger STAT state (border glow).
- Save & Continue promoted to a 52px CTA with shadow/hover-lift/
  ripple/arrow; Save Draft demoted to a plain text-style action so
  it doesn't compete with the primary CTA. Draft click now has real
  (mocked) saving/saved feedback instead of doing nothing.
- Full keyboard workflow: Ctrl/Cmd+F focuses search, Up/Down
  navigates the test list, Enter adds the highlighted/first-match
  test, Delete removes the most recently added test, Ctrl/Cmd+S
  saves a draft, Ctrl/Cmd+Enter continues to billing.
- Micro-interactions: row hover lift + price brighten, animated
  check pop on selection, Grand Total pulses on change, button
  ripple on the primary CTA.

Deliberately not done (needs product/data decisions, not just UI):
- Drag-to-reorder selected tests — selection order today is fixed
  by catalogue order, not insertion order; real reordering needs a
  small state change in PatientFlowService shared by Billing and
  Sample Collection, so it's safer as its own follow-up.
- Sidebar workflow grouping/connector lines — shared layout
  component used by every page, out of scope for a single-screen
  patch.
